test/check/error-layer-ownership.sumspec:10:25:
   |
10 | __init :: App(Mode.On * core.Core(core.Link.Down))
   |                         ^
core.Core is core's state, which starts at core's __init; leave it out of __init

test/check/error-layer-ownership.sumspec:15:39:
   |
15 | reset :: App => Mode.On -> Mode.Off * core.Core(core.Link.Down)
   |                                       ^
core.Core is core's state, which only core's events change; leave it out of the target, and fire one of them with >>

test/check/error-layer-ownership.sumspec:16:39:
   |
16 | prime :: App => Mode.On -> Mode.Off * core.Core'
   |                                       ^
core.Core is core's state, which only core's events change; leave it out of the target, and fire one of them with >>

test/check/error-layer-ownership.sumspec:17:25:
   |
17 | write core.TodoId#id :: core.Todos[id] => core.Completion.Active -> core.Completion.Completed
   |                         ^
core.Todos is part of core's state, which only core's events change; write the transition on this spec's state and fire one of them with >>

test/check/error-layer-ownership.sumspec:18:15:
   |
18 | link :: App / core.Core => core.Link.Up -> core.Link.Down
   |               ^
core.Core is core's state, which only core's events change; leave it out of the target, and fire one of them with >>

